# Raw per-cell run directories are session output, not artefacts of it: one
# `python cell/run_ladder_cell.py` writes transcripts, frame dumps, a copied
# workspace_container/ and phase-B telemetry, and 365 such files reached 227 MB
# before anyone noticed this file was missing. Every sibling benchmark
# directory has had one of these; ladder did not, which is how the output got
# committed in the first place.
#
# The REDUCED measurements -- the ones a reader would cite and the only ones
# any tracked code reads -- are allowlisted below:
#   rows.jsonl        cell_progress.py:145 globs */rows.jsonl for the historical
#                     median; test_ladder_cell.py:794 asserts on one of them.
#   cell_report.json  cell_progress.py:176 reads .workspace from it.
#   cell_report.md    the human-readable twin.
#   verdict.json      cell_progress.py:75 "graded" milestone.
#
# `!/results/**/` re-includes DIRECTORIES at every depth. Without it git never
# descends into results/ and none of the allowlists below can ever match --
# a bare `results/` would silently ignore the four kept files too.
#
# Anything else worth keeping (a doc-cited transcript, say) needs `git add -f`.
# This affects FUTURE output only; .gitignore never untracks what is already in.
/results/**
!/results/**/
!/results/**/rows.jsonl
!/results/**/verdict.json
!/results/**/cell_report.json
!/results/**/cell_report.md
